{"Buj": [{"id": "Buj", "headword": "भुज्", "headword_slp1": "Buj", "fold": "Buj", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "भुज् (I) vt. 6P (pp. भुग्न; pres. भुजति) To bend, to curve, to make crooked.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भुज् (II) vt. 7U (pp. भुक्त; pres. भुनक्ति, भुंक्ते; caus. भोजयति-ते; desid. बुभुक्षति-ते) 1. (Atm.) To eat, to consume, श्रेयो भोक्तुं भैक्ष्यमपीह लोके Bg.ii.5, शाल्यन्नं सघृतं पयोदधियुतं ये भूम्जते मानवास्तेषामिंद्रियनिग्रहो यदि भवेद्बिंध्यस्तरेत् सागरम् Bhartr.i.66, M.iii.146, iv.65; 2. (Atm.) to enjoy; 3. to enjoy carnally, सुरूपं वा विरूपं वा पुमानित्येव भुंजते M.ix.14; 4. (Par.) to rule, to govern, (धरित्रीं एकः कुत्स्यां नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति Sak.ii., R.iv.7; 5. to suffer, to endure, e.g. तस्यां तस्यामवरस्थायां भुंक्ते जन्मनि जन्मनि; 6. to pass (as time).With अनु-, 1. to endure, to experience; 2. to enjoy, अन्वभुंक्त स चंद्रिकाम् R.xix.39; 3. to pass through (in astronomy).With उप-, 1. to eat, अर्धोपभुक्तेन बिसेन जायां संभावयामास रथांगनामा K.S.iii.37, R.ii.65; 2. to enjoy; 3. to enjoy carnally, e.g. या न वेश्येव सामान्या पथिकैरुपभुज्यते; 4. to endure, to suffer, M.xii.8.With परि-, 1. to eat; 2. to enjoy, सुरवधूपरिभुक्तलतागृहाः Kir.v.5.With सम्-, 1. to eat; 2. to enjoy; 3. to enjoy carnally.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भुज् (I) a. (at the end of a compound) 1. Eating, enjoying, e.g. स्वधाभुज्, अमृतभुज्; 2. ruling, governing, e.g. क्षितिभुज्.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "भुज् (II) f. 1. Enjoyment; 2. profit, advantage.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "Buja": [{"id": "Buja", "headword": "भुज", "headword_slp1": "Buja", "fold": "Buja", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "भुज m. 1. The arm, भुजे भुजंगेंद्रसमानसारे R.ii.74, i.34, ii.23, iii.5; 2. the hand; 3. the trunk of an elephant; 4. a side of any mathematical figure; 5. the base of a triangle.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["भुजः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["BujaH"]}, {"id": "BujA", "headword